---
description: Treat user interruptions as useful in-flight guidance
alwaysApply: true
---

# User Interruptions

- When the user interrupts an ongoing action, treat the interruption as potentially useful new information for that action.
- Incorporate the new information into the current work instead of treating the interruption as a stop signal by default.
- After answering the interruption, continue the underlying task unless the user explicitly changes scope or asks to stop.
- For active troubleshooting, prefer updating the current plan/run with the new information over restarting from scratch.
